  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n3,\\,18,\\,11,\\,8,\\,7,\\,18,\\,12\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (3+18+11+8+7+18+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 77 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot ({3}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{11}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{18}^{2}+{12}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (9+324+121+64+49+324+144) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 1035 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{\u2015}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{\u2015}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-{(11)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1035}{7}-121 \\\\  & =\\frac{1035-847}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{188}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
